    {
      "id": "sec_n2vqwj7da4",
      "preset": "component/pw-statement@1",
      "label": "Statement section (The Pattern)",
      "anchor": "pattern",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "full"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "dark",
        "padding": {
          "d": "none",
          "m": "none"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_p8r06f0agr",
          "type": "component/pw-statement",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "closing": "Power With makes the pattern visible while it can still change.",
            "closingSize": "standard",
            "ground": "oxblood",
            "headline": "The drive that builds companies can dismantle marriages.",
            "headlineSize": "standard",
            "kicker": "THE PATTERN",
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "text": "Most people treat their success and their relational struggles as separate problems. The career is going well. The marriage is hard. Both run on the same operating system."
              },
              {
                "text": "The strategies that win in competition are specific. Control, self-sufficiency, the refusal to be affected, the need to stay ahead. At home and on a team, those same strategies create distance. The cost builds so slowly that most people see it only once it runs deep."
              }
            ],
            "subhead": "The control that commands respect can silence the people who love you most. The armor that makes you formidable can make you unreachable.",
            "width": "narrow"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec_raabxxcvxz",
      "preset": "component/pw-cards@1",
      "label": "Cards section (Framework, Authority, Organizations)",
      "anchor": "framework",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "full"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "light",
        "padding": {
          "d": "none",
          "m": "none"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_0rhqfqr5rj",
          "type": "component/pw-cards",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "buttonStyle": "primary",
            "cardStyle": "terms",
            "cards": [
              {
                "body": "Every conversation shapes one. Every meeting, every dinner and every decision shapes the trust and safety of the people around you. You hold more power than you may realize.",
                "definition": "Power is the capacity to shape outcomes.",
                "emphasis": false,
                "icon": "circle",
                "label": "POWER"
              },
              {
                "body": "It can look like competence, decisiveness and strength. In a crisis it has its place. As a default it produces distance, distrust and isolation, slowly, beneath a life that still looks highly functional.",
                "definition": "Power over is the use of influence to control.",
                "emphasis": false,
                "icon": "power-over",
                "label": "POWER OVER"
              },
              {
                "body": "It holds authority and relationship at the same time. You lead, decide and act while staying connected to the people your choices affect. It is the more disciplined orientation, and it asks more of you than power over ever did.",
                "definition": "Power with is the use of influence to stay in relationship.",
                "emphasis": false,
                "icon": "power-with",
                "label": "POWER WITH"
              }
            ],
            "closing": "The trust you build carries forward in your absence. That is lasting influence.",
            "closingSize": "large",
            "ground": "bone",
            "headline": "A language for power.",
            "headlineSize": "large",
            "intro": "Three terms carry the whole book. They are simple to define. Once you hold them, you see every relationship, every team and every room differently.",
            "kicker": "THE FRAMEWORK"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec_1sp4tm9k78",
      "preset": "component/pw-benefits@1",
      "label": "Benefits section (quote, columns, list)",
      "anchor": "what-changes",
      "layout": {
        "mode": "stack",
        "columns": {
          "d": [
            12
          ]
        },
        "width": "full"
      },
      "style": {
        "colorTheme": "dark",
        "padding": {
          "d": "none",
          "m": "none"
        }
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "blk_9mdrvgf99t",
          "type": "component/pw-benefits",
          "v": 1,
          "fields": {
            "closing": "These patterns took decades to form. The book gives you a clear map and practices to return to, one conversation at a time.",
            "columns": [
              {
                "body": "Your partner reaches for you. Your children bring you what is hard as well as what is impressive. Conflict ends in repair, and the distance between you begins to close.",
                "label": "AT HOME"
              },
              {
                "body": "People tell you what is actually happening. They commit to decisions they helped shape. Your best people stay, and the way your team works holds when you are out of the room.",
                "label": "AT WORK"
              },
              {
                "body": "The exhaustion of holding it all together begins to lift. You can be wrong and stay steady. You can be affected and remain intact.",
                "label": "WITHIN YOU"
              }
            ],
            "ground": "obsidian",
            "headline": "Power and closeness, held together.",
            "headlineSize": "standard",
            "items": [
              {
                "text": "Recognize the defended patterns running beneath your success, and the moment they take over."
              },
              {
                "text": "Stay present in the conversations you used to win, avoid or end."
              },
              {
                "text": "Acknowledge impact before you explain intent."
              },
              {
                "text": "Repair after rupture, so trust grows stronger through conflict."
              },
              {
                "text": "Lead from relational authority, the kind people follow by choice."
              },
              {
                "text": "Use the pause, the thirty seconds that change what you say next."
              }
            ],
            "kicker": "WHAT THIS BOOK GIVES YOU",
            "listLabel": "WHAT YOU WILL LEARN TO DO",
            "quote": "My intent in writing this book is to support you in becoming more powerful than you have ever been, while building the quality of relationships your life actually depends on.",
            "quoteBy": "SOPHIA LIFE"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
